{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EjZnHJ1LBCFxHntfrzqhX1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\timport Mathlib\n2\t\n3\topen MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Classical\n4\t\n5\tnoncomputable abbrev putnam_2022_a4_solution : ℝ := 2*Real.exp ((1 : ℝ) / 2) - 3\n6\t\n7\t/--\n8\tSuppose $X_1, X_2, ...$ real numbers between 0 and 1 that are chosen independently and uniformly at random. Let $S = \\sum_{i=1}^k X_i / 2^i $ where $k$ is the least positive integer such that $X_k < X_{k+1}$ or $k = \\infty$ if there is no such integer. Find the expected value of $S$\n9\t-/\n10\ttheorem putnam_2022_a4\n11\t    {Ω : Type*} [MeasureSpace Ω]\n12\t    [IsProbabilityMeasure (ℙ : Measure Ω)]\n13\t    (X : ℕ → Ω → ℝ)\n14\t    (hX : ∀ i, Measurable (X i))\n15\t    (hX' : ∀ i, MeasureTheory.pdf.IsUniform (X i) (Set.Icc 0 1) ℙ)\n16\t    (hX'' : iIndepFun X)\n17\t    (k : Ω → Set ℕ)\n18\t    /-\n19\t    If there is an `l` such that `X_l < X_{l+1}` then this is `Set.Iic l` for the smallest such `l`\n20\t    Otherwise, this is `sSup { (Set.Iic m : Set ℕ) | (m : ℕ) } = Set.univ`\n21\t    -/\n22\t    (hk : ∀ ω, k ω = sSup { s : Set ℕ |\n23\t      ∃ m, s = Set.Iic m ∧ ∀ l, l < m → X l ω > X (l + 1) ω })\n24\t    (S : Ω → ℝ)\n25\t    (hS : ∀ ω, S ω = ∑' (i : k ω), (X i ω) / (2 ^ (i.val + 1))) :\n26\t    ∫ ω, S ω ∂(ℙ : Measure Ω) = putnam_2022_a4_solution := by\n27\t  sorry\n28\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1aabaaa2-4949-4fb7-9c5b-10e92dc12121","uuid":"4bb112cf-e269-4cd3-9fb3-903746452712","timestamp":"2026-10-14T03:09:33.055Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/work/putnam_2022_a4.lean","content":"import Mathlib\n\nopen MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Classical\n\nnoncomputable abbrev putnam_2022_a4_solution : ℝ := 2*Real.exp ((1 : ℝ) / 2) - 3\n\n/--\nSuppose $X_1, X_2, ...$ real numbers between 0 and 1 that are chosen independently and uniformly at random. Let $S = \\sum_{i=1}^k X_i / 2^i $ where $k$ is the least positive integer such that $X_k < X_{k+1}$ or $k = \\infty$ if there is no such integer. Find the expected value of $S$\n-/\ntheorem putnam_2022_a4\n    {Ω : Type*} [MeasureSpace Ω]\n    [IsProbabilityMeasure (ℙ : Measure Ω)]\n    (X : ℕ → Ω → ℝ)\n    (hX : ∀ i, Measurable (X i))\n    (hX' : ∀ i, MeasureTheory.pdf.IsUniform (X i) (Set.Icc 0 1) ℙ)\n    (hX'' : iIndepFun X)\n    (k : Ω → Set ℕ)\n    /-\n    If there is an `l` such that `X_l < X_{l+1}` then this is `Set.Iic l` for the smallest such `l`\n    Otherwise, this is `sSup { (Set.Iic m : Set ℕ) | (m : ℕ) } = Set.univ`\n    -/\n    (hk : ∀ ω, k ω = sSup { s : Set ℕ |\n      ∃ m, s = Set.Iic m ∧ ∀ l, l < m → X l ω > X (l + 1) ω })\n    (S : Ω → ℝ)\n    (hS : ∀ ω, S ω = ∑' (i : k ω), (X i ω) / (2 ^ (i.val + 1))) :\n    ∫ ω, S ω ∂(ℙ : Measure Ω) = putnam_2022_a4_solution := by\n  sorry\n","numLines":28,"startLine":1,"totalLines":28}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EjZnHJ1LBCFxHntfrzqhX1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
